  {
   "say": "One Israeli, on average, produces as much as sixteen Egyptians.",
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Same region. Same sun. Let's line up the neighbours.",
   "screen": "GDP per person, *2024*",
   "at": "L1:let's",
   "until": "L8",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Saudi Arabia, sitting on oil: one Israeli equals one and a half Saudis.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Iraq: about nine.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Lebanon: ten. Jordan: eleven.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Egypt: sixteen.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Syria, after years of war: fifty six.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Yemen, torn by war: two hundred and seventy three.",
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "And it isn't oil. Natural resources bring in zero point one percent of Israel's economy. In Iraq, forty percent.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Only Qatar makes more per person. The Emirates come close.",
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "So what's our secret? Israelis just love to work. To build. To make something new, every single morning.",
   "screen": "Israelis *love* to build",
   "until": "L11",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "But this isn't about people. Talent is everywhere. Most of this gap is war, and how countries are run.",
   "screen": "Talent is *everywhere*",
   "until": "L12",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Income per person isn't happiness, and it isn't anyone's worth. Send this to someone who thinks it's all about resources.",
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Because it all starts with one person.",
   "gap": 0.15
  }
 ],
